# Sources reach every clone byte-identical.
#
# This is not cosmetic for a contracts repository: solc hashes the source text into the contract
# metadata, so a clone checked out with CRLF compiles to a different metadata hash than one checked
# out with LF. The bytecode verification on a block explorer then fails against a build made on
# another machine, and the cause is invisible in a diff.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Foundry's lockfile and the deployment records are read by tooling, never by a human editor.
foundry.lock text eol=lf
deployments/**/*.json text eol=lf
